# Accessibility Standards

Role: Accessibility Reviewer. Conform to WCAG 2.2 Level AA and ADA-aligned best practices.

## Semantics and ARIA
- Use semantic HTML elements and native controls first.
- Use ARIA only when required; do not add ARIA to elements that already have correct native semantics (avoid redundant ARIA).

## Keyboard
- Logical tab order
- Visible focus indicators
- Enter/Space activation for buttons and custom controls
- Escape to close dismissible overlays where applicable

## Motion
- Support `prefers-reduced-motion`: provide non-animated or minimally animated alternatives for all animations.

## Color and Content
- Sufficient contrast
- Do not rely on color alone to convey meaning
- Meaningful alt text; decorative images use `alt=""`

## Forms
- Every input must have an associated label
- Accessible error messaging (`aria-describedby`) and state (`aria-invalid`) when appropriate

## Dynamic UI
- Use ARIA live regions only when necessary and scope them appropriately.
